in @prism

in @optics
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens
in @mirror/lens/cli
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @mirror/lens/cli/time — Elm-style time travel as a stage.
#
# Seventh of eight verb sub-stages forward-promised in
# docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3 (table at §3 + §3.1 shape sketch).
# Realizes the tick-manifold view (Elm-style time travel) at the
# stage altitude — the substrate level where the named loop
# (focus → project → shift → settle) walks history.
#
# === Why time is a stage, and revert dissolved into it ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §2.1 + §5.3 (where time sang): `revert` was
# previously a single five-op surface in the cybernetic CLI; the
# recursive condensation DISSOLVED it into ONE OPERATION on the time
# manifold. `time settle tick=N` IS revert — write a new tick whose
# manifold matches tick N. The other four ops were already
# structurally present on the time manifold but not exposed by the
# `revert` framing; the recursion revealed more time-algebra than
# the cybernetic CLI had named. The substrate's tick type (declared
# in shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror as `type tick =
# monotonic`) carries the graph shape (ticks → ticks) that makes the
# five ops fit cleanly.
#
# === Substrate composition map (Seam, cli-as-prism §2.1) ===
#
# The 5-op surface condenses `boot/std/time.mirror`'s 9 actions:
#   focus    ← enter
#   shift    ← browse + step
#   split    ← fork
#   settle   ← restore (composed across the ref-set of tick N)
#   project  ← timeline.snapshots filtered by predicate
# The substrate already carries the algebra. Full
# `@epistemologic/reality/time` (proof-block shape + crack-interaction
# semantics) is Track G, deferred per LRM. This stage's actions are
# the CLI surface above the existing 9-action substrate; the
# composition lands when Track G fills in the proof shape.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Parent bench: @mirror/lens/cli (shards/mirror/lens/cli.mirror).
# Family root:  @mirror/lens    (shards/mirror/lens.mirror).
# Sibling stages:
#   @mirror/lens/cli/compile    — landed at 737330f
#   @mirror/lens/cli/kintsugi   — landed at ce2ef9b
#   @mirror/lens/cli/shatter    — landed at 9bc68f8
#   @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap  — landed at ea9c9a7
#   @mirror/lens/cli/sh         — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/reflect    — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/crack      — kintsugi geometry (next this tick)
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/cli/time.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/lens/cli/time` and only that.
#
# === Note: no mirror.spec command yet ===
#
# Unlike compile / kintsugi / shatter, time does NOT yet have a
# `command time { ... }` declaration in mirror.spec — the
# time-travel surface is consumed by the runtime's tick-manifold
# walker directly rather than the mosaic build dispatch. This stage
# shard is the CLI surface forward-promised by cli-as-prism.md §3;
# the mirror.spec-side declaration is a subsequent Taut tick
# (forward-promise: when `mirror.spec` gains a `command time
# { ... }` block, its arg shape carries the `tick=N` form this
# stage's actions already declare).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3, §3.1 (shape sketch),
#               §2.1 (time row: per-op decisions + substrate
#               composition map for the 9 boot/std/time.mirror
#               actions),
#               §5.3 (where time sang — revert dissolved),
#               §7 (default-op rule: time declares `default focus`
#               — reading history is free; settle is the revert
#               write),
#               docs/specs/the-convergence.md §2 (the four-lens
#               table row for `mirror time settle tick=N`),
#               docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.2 (stage).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
#                      (stage IS a sub-prism specialization),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
#                      (file path matches namespace),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (shift =
#                      basis transformation; here, the Elm scrub:
#                      see FROM tick N without moving HEAD).
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (parent bench),
#                 epistemologic/reality/time.mirror (the typed
#                 `tick = monotonic` carrier this stage walks; the
#                 substrate already carries the type-level guarantee
#                 that ticks compose only with ticks),
#                 glass.mirror (imperfect / transparency carriers).

stage @mirror/lens/cli/time {
  # Per cli-as-prism §7: time declares `default focus` — reading
  # history is free. Bare `mirror time` looks at state at the
  # current tick (a no-op focus showing HEAD). The settle path is
  # the revert write — a real substrate-state side effect (a new
  # tick whose manifold matches tick N); the user pays only for the
  # explicit settle. The other read-shaped ops (project / split /
  # shift) walk history without writing.
  default focus

  # The five operations the produced prism exposes on the time
  # sub-manifold (the tick graph; ticks → ticks with monotonic
  # ordering per epistemologic/reality/time.mirror). Each operand
  # below names the natural shape of the manifold's element at that
  # op's slot, per the spec §3.1 sketch convention and §2.1's
  # per-verb decisions:
  #   focus    tick        — look at state at tick N (read past;
  #                          no write); tick is the typed monotonic
  #                          carrier from epistemologic/reality/time
  #   project  predicate   — filter history by predicate (composes
  #                          with timeline.snapshots per the Seam
  #                          composition map at cli-as-prism §2.1)
  #   split    tick        — branch a parallel timeline from tick N
  #                          (composes with the substrate's fork
  #                          action)
  #   shift    tick        — see FROM tick N without moving HEAD
  #                          (the Elm scrub; basis transformation
  #                          on the tick manifold;
  #                          [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]];
  #                          composes with browse + step)
  #   settle   tick        — the ONE write; write a new tick whose
  #                          manifold matches tick N (this IS revert;
  #                          composes with the substrate's restore
  #                          across the ref-set of tick N); emits
  #                          proof block recording the time-write
  focus    tick
  project  predicate
  split    tick
  shift    tick
  settle   tick
}

# === Time-specific actions ===
#
# No mirror.spec `command time { ... }` declaration yet (see the
# "no mirror.spec command yet" note above). The CLI surface action
# signature lands here as the substrate forward-promise; the Rust
# runtime walks this declaration when the time-travel surface lifts
# into the mosaic dispatch. Substrate-pull discipline per
# [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]].
#
# Honest `partials` from birth (per recognition #306): the return
# type is the substrate's `imperfect` functor (declared in
# shards/glass.mirror as `imperfect(a, e, l) = success(a) |
# partial(a, l) | failure(e, l)`). A clean revert returns success
# carrying the new HEAD tick ref; a revert that lifts loss (e.g. a
# crack interaction — a fracture declared between tick N and HEAD
# whose state cannot be cleanly carried backward) returns
# partial-with-loss carrying the transparency-tagged residual
# opacity; a hard failure (tick out of bounds, ref-set unresolvable)
# returns failure. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: the tick arg is
# the substrate's typed `tick` (declared at
# `@epistemologic/reality/time/tick` as `type tick = monotonic`), not
# a bare int. The crack-interaction semantics are Track G; this
# stage's partial shape forward-promises the carrier.

# time_focus(tick) — look at state at tick N (read past; no write).
# Returns the imperfect carrying the historical state ref on success;
# partial-with-loss on tolerable read shortfall (e.g. tick exists but
# one ref in its set could not be reconstructed); failure on tick out
# of bounds.
time_focus(tick: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# time_revert(tick) — write a new tick whose manifold matches tick N
# (this IS revert per cli-as-prism §5.3 dissolution). Composes with
# the substrate's restore action across the ref-set of tick N.
# Returns the imperfect carrying the new HEAD tick ref on success;
# partial-with-loss on tolerable revert shortfall (e.g. a crack
# interaction Track-G semantics will close); failure on hard write
# error.
time_revert(tick: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

out @mirror/lens/cli/time
out time_focus
out time_revert
